# Hama, the Bloodbender's "you may cast the exiled card during your turn by waterbending {X} rather than paying its mana cost"
# (CR 701.67a-b, 118.9) for a card with improvise (CR 702.126a): Metallic Rebuke, mana value 3, is exiled, and on turn three
# Bot1 has {U}{U} floating (an Island and Mox Sapphire) and an untapped Hama, its Mox Ruby spent on a Lightning Bolt and no
# artifact left untapped for improvise. The waterbend {3} is paid by the {U}{U} and tapping Hama, a creature, which improvise
# could not tap: both may help pay, each permanent tapped for one of them (CR 601.2h). The Rebuke counters the Bolt, whose
# controller has nothing left to pay {3} with, so Bot2 stays at 20.

